 "researcher_notes": "MATCH CHECK: no roster row for this line; P1476 Makat-North Caucasus (944 km, trunk) is the parent it taps; P3972 Kharabali-Akhtubinsk 2-Akhtubinsk 1 (179.5 km, proposed) is the separate onward second-stage line from Kharabali (nz206 describes it as a distinct 180.8 km project in design). Not a duplicate of either. CONFIRMED: Gazprom-built gas branch (decision per 2012 Gazprom-Astrakhan govt agreement; first weld 16 Sep 2016; steel pipe 500 mm, 79.6 km per neftegaz 2017 [79.9 km planned per neftegaz 2016; 79 km laid by Oct 2017; astrg 2018 says 80 km]; 3 GRS at Khosheutovo, Volnoye, Kharabali). Harabali-vst 2022-07-04: Gazprom fully completed construction of the branch in 2021; astrg Aug 2018 says GRS Volnoye/Kharabali due March 2019 -> StartYear1 2021 taken from the 2022 article (medium on exact year; line was physically laid by 2018). Window: operating line never captured -> qualifies; length 79.6 km >= 25 km sourced; sponsor Gazprom; concrete step = built/completed. Cost not entered: neftegaz gives >3 bn RUB construction-works only vs 12 bn RUB total Gazprom investment (2016) - inconsistent scopes. Capacity not stated in any source. Owner by inference from 'Gazprom completed construction/investment' - no separate operator found (Gazprom Gazoraspredeleniye Astrakhan is the downstream distribution entity; entity_lookup shows Gazprom PJSC exists). Route: none sourced; no official GIS checked/found - leave no route for routes leg. Tier high: 3 independent publishers (neftegaz, Gazprom Mezhregiongaz Astrakhan site, Kharabalinskie vesti) agree on length/diameter/name; neftegaz 2016/2017 pieces both trace to Astrakhan government press releases, so independence counted via astrg + vst."
